# loom and C11 (verus/WEAKMEM.md, P4): `STATE.word` has two writes,
# `state_claim`'s exchange and `state_publish`'s `READY` store
# (tests/loom/tests/access.rs), so its modification order is `UNINIT`,
# `INITIALISING`, `READY`, each written once, and the permission's value
# reads as the last of them. C++20's exchange is a read-modify-write,
# which reads the last value for every ordering ([atomics.order] p10), in
# the strong form, which fails only when the value differs; a load reads a
# write no older than the last one that happens before it (coherence,
# [intro.races]); the `Release` store of `READY` with an `Acquire` load or
# exchange that reads it orders `init`'s plain writes before the reader (a
# release/acquire pair, [atomics.order] p2). The init models check this on
# a copy of `init_slow`, `shared` and `shared_if_ready` (`STATE`,
# `INIT_TID` and `SHARED` are statics built in `const` context, which loom
# cannot construct). The GenMC flags cases copy the two bodies' atomic
# lines, `STATE`'s `Acquire` load and `READY` store, onto `core`'s atomic,
# pinned to these bodies (tests/genmc/flags.rs, `GENMC_PINS`), as the
# publication of `put_flags`' writes to the dispatch byte's readers. The
# GenMC init cases (tests/genmc/init.rs) copy the init steps themselves,
# `init_slow`, `shared` and `shared_if_ready`, onto `core`'s atomics,
# pinned to these bodies in `GENMC_PINS` the same way.
state_load	atomics primitive	loom/GenMC	trusted (partly checked, loom: init::loom_init_free_races_init, init::loom_init_two_callers, init::loom_init_reentry_aborts and init::loom_init_publisher_reads_ready, and GenMC: flags1 [rc11 imm], flags2 [rc11 imm arm8], init3 [rc11+live imm+live arm8+live] and init3_readback [rc11+live imm+live]; not checked: this body, which the models replace with loom's `load` inside a copy of the init steps, with the callers tests/loom/src/init.rs states, and the GenMC cases with `core`'s `load` (a line tests/loom/tests/pins.rs pins to this body's) inside a copy of the dispatch byte's steps, which publishes `put_flags`' writes only, and inside a copy of the init steps with the callers tests/genmc/init.rs states (up to three, two waiting at once), each case only under the memory models its citation names (verus/WEAKMEM.md, "GenMC": no race report under ARMv8, and the `-Copt-level=1` IR, not the release build); the callers neither copy has, and what `init` writes besides the one value the copies publish, which no case runs; the C11 argument above that the permission's value is `STATE.word`'s last write, which no GenMC case checks (the copy takes no permission) and tests/loom/tests/access.rs backs by matching source text only)	contract 3749283829, body 4146854669
state_claim	atomics primitive	loom/GenMC	trusted (partly checked, loom: init::loom_init_free_races_init, init::loom_init_two_callers and init::loom_init_reentry_aborts, and GenMC: init2 [rc11+live imm+live] and init3 [rc11+live imm+live arm8+live]; not checked: this body, which the models replace with loom's `compare_exchange` inside a copy of the init steps, with the callers tests/loom/src/init.rs states, and the GenMC cases with `core`'s `compare_exchange` (a line tests/loom/tests/pins.rs pins to this body's) inside a copy of the init steps, with the callers tests/genmc/init.rs states, each case only under the memory models its citation names (verus/WEAKMEM.md, "GenMC": no race report under ARMv8, and the `-Copt-level=1` IR, not the release build); that it never fails spuriously, which loom's compare-and-swap cannot show, GenMC's strong exchange assumes, and rests on `core`'s documentation of the strong form; the C11 argument above, which no GenMC case checks (the copy takes no permission) and tests/loom/tests/access.rs backs by matching source text only)	contract 85710167, body 3985027897
state_publish	atomics primitive	loom/GenMC	trusted (partly checked, loom: init::loom_init_free_races_init, init::loom_init_two_callers, init::loom_init_reentry_aborts and init::loom_init_publisher_reads_ready, and GenMC: flags1 [rc11 imm], flags2 [rc11 imm arm8], init3 [rc11+live imm+live arm8+live] and init3_readback [rc11+live imm+live]; not checked: this body, which the models replace with loom's `store` inside a copy of the init steps, with the callers tests/loom/src/init.rs states (the readback after the store is a load the model adds), and the GenMC cases with `core`'s `store` (a line tests/loom/tests/pins.rs pins to this body's) inside a copy of the dispatch byte's steps, which publishes `put_flags`' writes only, and inside a copy of the init steps with the callers tests/genmc/init.rs states (its readback is a load the harness adds too), each case only under the memory models its citation names (verus/WEAKMEM.md, "GenMC": no race report under ARMv8, and the `-Copt-level=1` IR, not the release build); what `init` writes besides the one value the copies publish, which no case runs; the C11 argument above, which no GenMC case checks (the copy takes no permission) and tests/loom/tests/access.rs backs by matching source text only)	contract 2256376580, body 1682955642
