# Termination of `init_slow`'s wait, given that `init` returns, a fair
# scheduler and that a store becomes visible in finite time (C++20
# [intro.progress] says it should): a waiter read `INITIALISING`, which
# only the one successful exchange writes, and that thread stores `READY`
# after `init`; were the waiter that thread, its `INIT_TID` load would
# read its own tid (read-after-write coherence) and it would abort. The
# init models check that no waiter is left spinning and that only the
# initialising thread takes the re-entry abort, on a copy.
init_slow	termination	loom/GenMC	trusted (partly checked, loom: init::loom_init_free_races_init, init::loom_init_two_callers and init::loom_init_reentry_aborts, and GenMC: init1 [rc11+live imm+live], init3 [rc11+live imm+live arm8+live] and init3_reenter [rc11+live imm+live]; not checked: this body, which the models replace with a copy, with the callers tests/loom/src/init.rs states and one waiter at a time, and the GenMC cases with a copy too (its lines pinned by tests/loom/tests/pins.rs), with the callers tests/genmc/init.rs states (up to three, two waiting at once), each case only under the memory models its citation names (verus/WEAKMEM.md, "GenMC": no race report under ARMv8, and the `-Copt-level=1` IR, not the release build); termination itself, which rests on `init` returning, a fair scheduler and visible stores, as loom models them and GenMC's liveness check (`+live`) assumes, and which that check cannot see for a wait the compiler emptied of loads (verus/WEAKMEM.md, "GenMC"); the fork gate (`init_gate_enter`, `init_gate_done`), which no case runs; a child forked while `init` runs, or a signal handler on the initialising thread that allocates before its `INIT_TID` store, spins for ever, outside the C contract)	contract 1867649379, body 4001748639
